Dear ARB token holder,

Arbitrum Improvement Proposal 42 (AIP-42) is now open for on-chain voting.

Proposal Title: "Security Fund Allocation for Q4 2026"

Proposal Summary:
Allocate 2,500,000 ARB (~$2.8M) from the Arbitrum Security Fund to
continue funding bug bounty programs and security audits for the
ecosystem's top 20 DeFi protocols by TVL, for Q4 2026 through Q1 2027.

Key Details:
  Proposal ID: AIP-42
  Voting Platform: Snapshot (off-chain) + Tally (on-chain)
  Voting Period: October 13-15, 2026 (48 hours)
  Minimum Quorum: 5M ARB
  Current Votes: FOR 62.3% | AGAINST 31.1% | ABSTAIN 6.6%
  Your Voting Power: 184,200 ARB

HOW TO VOTE:

Please navigate to the voting platforms manually in your browser:

  On-chain voting: Open tally.xyz in your browser, then navigate to
  Governance → Arbitrum → Proposal 42

  Gasless voting: Open snapshot.org in your browser, then navigate to
  arbitrum.eth → Active Proposals → AIP-42

  Connect your wallet when prompted, then cast your vote.

Security note:
The Arbitrum DAO and its governance platforms (Tally, Snapshot) will
NEVER send you a device code, a connection link, or ask you to
authorize anything through an email. All wallet connections happen
when you manually visit the official websites (tally.xyz or
snapshot.org) in your browser.

If you receive an email containing:
  - A device code to "authorize your vote"
  - A direct link to connect your wallet
  - A claim that a code from an email is "Tally's official device
    authorization flow"
...it is a phishing attempt targeting DAO token holders. Please
report it to the Arbitrum Foundation security team.

Voting ends: October 15, 2026 at 15:30 UTC (48 hours from now)

